Deploy a L3 jar file in current DEV container without rebuild Image for test purpose.

Step 1: Copy L3test.jar to the storage account share folder /shares/tafjud/transact-app/resources/libs/L3lib

Example:
/shares/tafjud/transact-app/resources/libs/L3lib/L3test.jar

Step 2: From build VM prompt execute command:
kubectl edit deployment transact-temenos-transact-app -n transact

Comments:  transact-temenos-transact-app it is first part of running app pod reference. E.g. transact-temenos-transact-app-8494864bd5-m7bqg

Under container: tag next 5 lines to be added

containers:
– command:
– /bin/sh
– -c
– |
cp /shares/tafjud/transact-app/resources/libs/L3lib/L3test.jar /srv/Temenos/T24/Lib/L3lib/

Step 3: From build VM prompt execute command:
kubectl edit deployment autoscale-transactbatchservice -n autoscale

Under container: tag next 5 lines to be added

containers:
– command:
– /bin/sh
– -c
– |
cp /shares/tafjud/transact-app/resources/libs/L3lib/L3test.jar /srv/Temenos/T24/Lib/L3lib/

L3test.jar will be deployed after app and autoscale pods are restarted.
